sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-21> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-21: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.445"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.52"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The timing of first appearance of species differences is measurable in public expression series for a few well-studied animals. That timing does not separate late origin of variation from early origin plus later inheritance or from selective removal of early changes. The mechanism as a general explanation of embryology is therefore only partly constrained by existing data, and extending it past model species would be a long compilation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Measure when, in ontogeny, differences among related species first appear in morphology and gene expression, and whether the genetic variants that distinguish them are expressed at that same later age. The claim is confirmed if species differences and their underlying variants are systematically late and embryos remain comparatively uniform, and refuted if most differences are already present at the earliest stages." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Early embryonic similarity can be produced by selection removing early variants, which yields the same pattern without variations originating late.", "Expression-timing and mapping data exist for a handful of model animals, not for animals generally.", "Showing that a variant is inherited at a corresponding age requires pedigrees or experimental crosses that are available for very few traits." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-21--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-21 by Grok 4.7: 0.5" ;
